  "adaptations": [
    "Native JUCE alternative layout with real processor controls, preset data and signals; no reference PNG is used as a background or implementation screenshot.",
    "Three independently visible oscillator cards use measured power, waveform, native wavetable-selector, four-control and tuning-row geometry. A power glyph edits actual oscillator mute; solo and key tracking retain their real parameters.",
    "Wavetable strips show the current native table and use the existing previous/catalog/next workflow. Non-wavetable algorithms remain accurately identified and cannot select an unavailable table; illustrated preset names are not fabricated.",
    "Oscillator controls retain current native algorithm names and dynamic parameter labels. The footer unison/remaining spread control binds oscillator 1 parameters 6/5, with their actual algorithm-dependent labels and availability. The second oscillator prioritizes parameter 5 (Classic unison detune); the third places parameter 1 before parameter 0 (FM2 M1 ratio then amount). These controls keep their actual current-algorithm labels after a type change.",
    "Filter A and B are the two filter units in the selected scene. Shared waveshaper drive and native filter balance retain truthful labels instead of claiming separate per-filter drive/mix stages. Additional filter subtype editing remains in the full editor.",
    "The amplitude and filter EGs remain independently visible. The third panel explicitly uses the real LFO 3 envelope and renders its ADSR stages; it is not a fictional third dedicated EG. The showcase filter EG uses a genuine 4 ms attack because the concept's 3.2 ms is below the native continuous-time range.",
    "LFO 1\u20134 tabs select the actual source and rebind shape, rate, phase, amplitude attack/fade, delay and trigger mode together. Changing the visible LFO does not change the sound.",
    "The vertical effects list provides eight independent real algorithm menus. Slot labels/status reflect actual effect state; the full native editor exposes all sixteen slots and their detailed controls.",
    "The compact signal-flow strip follows the native filter routing configuration, with no arbitrary cable-editing claim.",
    "Eight native macros follow the measured lower strip. Pitch/FM faders remain honestly bound to scene pitch and FM depth; real MIDI expression wheels require the native full editor.",
    "Voice mode is a genuine native menu rather than three inert Mono/Poly/Legato buttons. Scene mode, pan, drift and less prominent controls remain accessible through the full editor.",
    "Header preset, scene, skin and editor navigation remain functional. Materials, condensed headings and bevels are procedural native painting. Captures, keyboard/parameter behavior and scaling must be verified from a compiled current-source build; static validation does not establish pixel identity."
  ]
}
